# Local maintainer — no remote (detail)

Kernel lives in always-on `shared-checkout-worktree_ulg` (`¬push ∧ ¬pr`).

**Invariant:** `sole_maintainer_local ⇒ ¬push ∧ ¬gh_pr ∧ ¬ask(pr)` unless the operator
names that act ("push", "open a PR", `gh pr create`, "publish the branch").

| Forbidden | Permitted |
|---|---|
| `git push` / set upstream to publish | Local commits on a feature/worktree branch when commit is in scope |
| `gh pr create` / compare-URL as the review close | Local branch `@sha` + `git diff --stat <base>..HEAD` |
| "Should I open a PR?" | Stop after the local review package |

Commission briefs that say "feature branch + PR" do not override this — PR is optional
only when the operator asks for it in this conversation.
